<title>USA: Bucyrus says union ratifies agreement.</title>
<headline>Bucyrus says union ratifies agreement.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH MILWAUKEE, Wisc. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bucyrus International Inc said Wednesday that members of the United Steelworkers of America had voted to ratify a new four-year labor contract with the company.</p>
<p>The company and the union agreed to negotiate the contract four months early after an April announcement by Bucyrus that it entered a letter of intent to buy the assets of the Marion Power Shovel Co from Global Industrial Technologies.</p>
<p>The new labor contract expires on April 30, 2001.</p>
<p>Bucyrus manufactures surface mining equipment.</p>
</text>
